# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Remote media testing — copy to .env.tunnel and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.tunnel.example .env.tunnel
#   npm run tunnel
#
# Read on top of .env, overriding it, and only while `npm run tunnel` is running.
# Your .env is never modified, so normal development is unaffected.
#
# Why a cloud SFU instead of the local container: LiveKit publishes ICE
# candidates as `node-ip:port` and no tunnel rewrites them, so a tunnelled SFU
# hands the browser an address it cannot reach. The room connects, both avatars
# appear, and there is no audio. See docs/remote-media-testing.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── LiveKit Cloud ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three from ONE project at https://cloud.livekit.io — Settings → Keys.
# The free tier is enough for a two-person test.
#
# `npm run tunnel` calls listRooms() with these before starting anything, so a
# wrong secret stops the run instead of surfacing later as "we can see each
# other but nobody can hear anything".
#
# Named LIVEKIT_CLOUD_* rather than LIVEKIT_*, because .env already defines
# LIVEKIT_URL as ws://localhost:7880. Sharing the name would let a forgotten
# value here fall through to the local one — and the stack would start, look
# healthy, and hand every remote guest an address on their own machine.
LIVEKIT_CLOUD_URL=wss://your-project.livekit.cloud
LIVEKIT_CLOUD_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_CLOUD_API_SECRET=

# ── ngrok ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent must already hold an authtoken:
#
#   ngrok config add-authtoken <token>
#
# Optional. A reserved domain — the free tier includes one — keeps the guest's
# link working across restarts. Left empty, ngrok issues a new random URL every
# run and the script picks it up automatically; you just have to resend it.
# Host only, no scheme: e.g. calm-otter-42.ngrok-free.app
NGROK_DOMAIN=

# Optional. Only if the `ngrok` binary is not on PATH.
# NGROK_BIN=
